egory" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-8394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f82fa702c211b046081b0fcaee8c5a347d50545af66c632d5e643818e7988a1" "basis" 1023 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/df7a1eb6aaf75cc611826af00ce066ed05440bb048ad79d8c0532007b9a89c3a.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "f07b529fcc489010236892ec02a2f855802235483748b56921c87bff17bae15d" "basis" 1083 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =Ai=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =Aj=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/77936c4115b37d79ae301a93b218ecd23114ae4ad42d8298b8f058c1f50e82a2.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians **clockwise** about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ **clockwise** by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/assets/e941207a92a2b688428c55be3bc17856ea47fa2e11db8e3dc571b88ebbe8e3b1.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/state.json" "file_sha256" "f07b529fcc489010236892ec02a2f855802235483748b56921c87bff17bae15d" "basis" 1083 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-81829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003089/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5412300abaf3d9cfe40c7fe60724db3bf41b03e257c8e1c9aa4b8a19eb15cd3" "basis" 1083 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt